newrootfs
=========

A set of programs to download, extract and maintain rootfs of various
operating systems. usual use cases include chroot trees or diskless
environments.

currently there are two programs, both of which support NetBSD and OpenBSD:

getsets - downloads all file sets for a given release
extractsets - verify checksums and construct a skeleton rootfs from a
set downloaded with getsets

requirements
------------
sha512sum/sha256sum if you want to verify sets, bourne shell and xz (for 64bit NetBSD sets).

Supported NetBSD archs: aarch64, amd64 and earmv6hf and earmv7hf.
Supported OpenBSD archs: amd64, arm64 and armv7.

the program have primarly been tested on OpenBSD, but special care has been
given to make sure it is not dependent on OpenBSD.

see also
--------
https://github.com/cheusov/sets2rootfs
